{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge","id":1067106,"title":"Mages in the Hedge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-23T12:45:55-07:00","id":1067106,"title":"Mages in the Hedge","content":"How is magic affected in the Hedge if at all? I'm trying to find out in the books but don't see anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4045-princeofcincinnati","name":"princeofcincinnati","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4045_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T13:52:33-07:00","id":1067156,"title":"","content":"I believe it's function is more limited in the hedge for certain Arcana, like Time, but nothing has been specifically laid out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T22:54:59-07:00","id":1067420,"title":"","content":"1e had a fairly extensive list that can be summarized as &quot;things in the Hedge are affected by the Arcana that they appear to be (living things with Life, inanimate objects with Matter, etc) unless they're part of the Thorns,&quot; &quot;sensory magic has its dicepool capped by your Wisdom rating,&quot; and &quot;you cannot exit the Hedge except through a Hedge gate.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2e shifts some of this \u2014 Hedge Gates are subject to the same rules as other Irises, for instance, so a Master of Fate can leave the Hedge as readily as a Master of Death can escape the Underworld \u2014 but more detailed information will likely show up in the Crossover Chronicle eventually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:37:12-07:00","id":1067578,"title":"","content":"2e hedge you still need a hedge gate to leave, you can just use other forms of magic to enter the hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T09:02:51-07:00","id":1067628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1067578#post1067578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e hedge you still need a hedge gate to leave, you can just use other forms of magic to enter the hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2e five dots in Fate lets you <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/872952-a-changeling-related-question?p=873580#post873580\"><i>make a Hedge Gate</i></a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T10:55:10-07:00","id":1068344,"title":"","content":"Freaking mages. I really dislike how 2ed is &quot;mages do everything better than everyone else.&quot; There's powerful and then there's just... broken. The crossover book may have seriously unfun issues with mages involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T12:20:46-07:00","id":1068370,"title":"","content":"Think of it this way: mages may wield more power than most supernaturals, but they are also the most hamstrung by those powers, and everyone else also has a lot more finesse with their abilities. When mages mess up with flexing the universe, the universe flexes back, hard; I believe one example I read was that an archmage attempting to use a spell to heat a cup of tea could accidentally set the neighboring apartment on fire. The other supernaturals don't have nearly that scale of trouble should something go wrong with their powers (save for perhaps Demons, given the whole God-Machine situation).<br /> <br /> Likewise, remember that both Changelings and Sin-Eaters are capable of opening and even making their respective gates far easier than a Mage can create them. Mages need to be a master of the field to do so, whereas for the other supernaturals, it's all just one piece of their innate kit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T22:13:54-07:00","id":1068550,"title":"","content":"I'm not really assuaged. The Mage game just seems to shoehorn the entire WoD/ChronD universe into being mage- centric while at the same time saying &quot;oh well mArcadia and cArcadia are definitely two different things.&quot; If they're different, great, but have them be different. Stop letting the Fate mages stomp all over Changelings by controlling or changing their Oaths, or making Gates to the real world directly from the deep hedge gates of Arcadia. cArcadia and the Hedge could instead be its own thing, not a mage style realm neatly tucked in a little box that they can control on a whim, and the Wyrd should kick mages in the ass if they try to muck up the story It's telling no matter how much Fate magic the mage has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T23:28:28-07:00","id":1068559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1068550#post1068550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really assuaged. The Mage game just seems to shoehorn the entire WoD/ChronD universe into being mage- centric</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage's metaphysical deal is &quot;the source of Awakened power is built on symbolism, which every other supernatural force in the setting also makes use of because this is a storytelling game, and the Awakened collectively seek to understand as much of the supernatural world as possible and often trade secrets to this end.&quot; That's not &quot;the shared setting is Mage-centric,&quot; that's &quot;mages have been poking around in the vicinity of the center of the setting for pretty much as long as there have been mages, so they've taken a lot of notes that tend to mesh with the way the setting actually works.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is pretty much the only context in which I encounter the sharpshooter fallacy being used as the basis for a <i>complaint</i>, for the record.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> while at the same time saying &quot;oh well mArcadia and cArcadia are definitely two different things.&quot; If they're different, great, but have them be different. </div> </div> </div>This demand is, in fact, met. You may notice that the existence of the Durance as a phenomenon is not Solved\u2122 just because the Fate Arcanum exists, that the Hedge is more than its thresholds, and that Arcadia does not have the same level of open mutability as the place that separates it from Earth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Stop letting the Fate mages stomp all over Changelings by controlling or changing their Oaths, or making Gates to the real world directly from the deep hedge gates of Arcadia. </div> </div> </div>These powers first become available at the second-highest and highest levels of power in a single Arcanum, respectively, using them safely at <i>just</i> those levels effectively requires either extensive preparation or exceedingly short usage periods, and they cost resources to use for any mage that hasn't spent extra time and experience specializing in them.<br /> <br /> (Also, unless Fate is their only Arcanum at the necessary level to accomplish these things, they have to be sitting at a minimum of Gnosis 4 or 6, respectively, which substantially narrows the viability of saying &quot;Fate mages&quot; when you mean the rough Awakened equivalent of spirits that entire ecosystems are built around in Werewolf.)<br /> <br /> Also, Changeling pledgecraft doesn't generally have multiple trigger clauses and pretty much the entirety of Lost society is built of people who determined it was better to break a mystical binding than stay in a horrific situation. Sever Oaths is not fae kryptonite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> cArcadia and the Hedge could instead be its own thing, not a mage style realm neatly tucked in a little box that they can control on a whim, </div> </div> </div>Friend, I invite you to consider just how little influence it is to be able to use acquired mastery of the forces of destiny to <i>open a door to</i> the world of suffering that dreams nestle in in relation to the entire suite of abilities changelings get as an innate function of having been tampered with by the shifting land of the gods and the monsters therein.<br /> <br /> Opening a Hedge gate isn't going to let you force your way into a Dream Bastion or part the Thorns or instill a clearing with abiding essence of regret.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and the Wyrd should kick mages in the ass if they try to muck up the story It's telling no matter how much Fate magic the mage has. </div> </div> </div>It does. Less crude channels than blanket immunity are available to accomplish this task, most prominent among them being &quot;watch the beehive Merlin just poked turn out to be a lot more trouble than tweaking a solitary noble's vow might've indicated.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T00:08:07-07:00","id":1068569,"title":"","content":"I still find it weird that Hedge stuff is done by mages with Fate rather than Mind considering the realm is so psychoreactive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T06:28:29-07:00","id":1068638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1068569#post1068569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still find it weird that Hedge stuff is done by mages with Fate rather than Mind considering the realm is so psychoreactive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate is psychoactive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 03-27-2017, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T13:13:05-07:00","id":1069567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1068569#post1068569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still find it weird that Hedge stuff is done by mages with Fate rather than Mind considering the realm is so psychoreactive.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hedge is psychoreactive in a way that's a fair bit more granular than Mind typically gets, most of the fully mental stuff it deals with is in isolated pockets that occasionally manifest in ways outside the scope of the Awakened framework for imaginary constructs, and the place's loose interface with the waking world doesn't have any relation to the degrees of resonance and abstraction that other phenomena deal with \u2014 a Hedge gate can exist somewhere just because there happened to be a Hedge gate there, with no real environmental bleedthrough or warning signs besides direct artifacts of its usage (and in fact this is an established problem with one of 1e's sample Bridge Burner associations' attempts to shut down emergent trods; they can predict where a new Hedge gate will spontaneously arise with a decent degree of fidelity, but leveraging land development to try and throw off whatever process causes them specifically doesn't work).<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Hedge has easy roads and hard roads and is occupied by things both really want and really don't want \u2014 and the Fate Arcanum deals with intention and desire. This is the border march that lesser djinn inhabit, and negotiating it is a function of what you're prepared to go through and how clever you are about your choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T04:56:21-07:00","id":1070577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1068559#post1068559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Changeling pledgecraft doesn't generally have multiple trigger clauses and pretty much the entirety of Lost society is built of people who determined it was better to break a mystical binding than stay in a horrific situation. Sever Oaths is not fae kryptonite.</div> </div> </div> </div> For the record, Oathbreaker is a very, very serious Condition. Changing an Oath so that a changeling has to either abide by the new or lose their Court / Freehold/etc? That's big. Its not an automatic win button, but its definitely something that can be crippling. And a lot of Awakened magics drawbacks do have ways around them.<br /> <br /> Of course, trying to affect a Changeling that's got Abjuration or has Embraced the Wyrd to raise their Resistances (and thus Withstand?) can pretty much shrug off mage magic on top of that spend-willpower-to-raise-withstand-by-clairty-dots bit. And good luck trying to counter a changeling using a contract (playtesting has shown some rather huge dice pools being thrown about). There's been a lot of reaction against the Mage design of dominating over other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> And its not a given that there's a gateway spell to get out. In 1e, it was explicitly forbidden as a feature of the Hedge by any sort of magic, Awakened, Contract, whatever. That rule, if it exists in 2e, takes precidence over anything a Master of Fate can do. You'll need Archmaster to get around that.<br /> <br /> Mages can do a lot of things, but on the other hand, they can't do everything either if there's a powerful magic force telling them no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-30-2017, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T10:57:06-07:00","id":1070747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1070577#post1070577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For the record, Oathbreaker is a very, very serious Condition. Changing an Oath so that a changeling has to either abide by the new or lose their Court / Freehold/etc? That's big.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also not the kind of oath that a mage is going to know about casually, and the fact that pledgesmithing is a moderately common role among changelings means it's going to become clear pretty quickly that something is up even if the Adept or Master in question was wise enough not to make this change obvious.<br /> <br /> Iif a changeling has somehow attracted the attention of a mage that's delved so deeply into the Mysteries of Fate that they can alter their pledges long-term <i>and</i> that mage has managed to learn enough about the changeling that they know the terms of one of their most significant oaths well enough to rewrite them <i>and</i> that mage is sufficiently subtle that all the resources available to a changeling aren't enough to track them down and/or render the spell ineffective, either there's a <i>story</i> behind that or there's a massive asymmetry at play that has nothing to do with splat parity<br /> <br /> In the meantime, most relevant instances of Sever Oaths being used against the Lost are going to amount to Contract countermagic, twisting and negating Sealings, or messing with oaths whose parties can be counted on one hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And its not a given that there's a gateway spell to get out. </div> </div> </div>The Hedge is not <i>that </i>special and it is actively detrimental to Changeling's presentation to try to make it so considering how much space 1e already wasted on playing up the Arcadia Problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In 1e, it was explicitly forbidden as a feature of the Hedge by any sort of magic, Awakened, Contract, whatever. </div> </div> </div>I'm aware. 1e also had a lot of problems with encouraging exactly the sort of baggage-with-Mage that Changeling <i>does not need</i>, to say nothing of how entry into the Hedge already constitutes a much less restricted form of extradimensional movement than most other games' supernatural otherworlds.<br /> <br /> Mastery of Fate is <i>past</i> the level where you can alter the terms of supernatural agreements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That rule, if it exists in 2e, takes precidence over anything a Master of Fate can do. You'll need Archmaster to get around that. </div> </div> </div>A Master of Death can form the conditions needed for an Avernian Gate to come into existence despite those conditions normally calling for drastic adjustment of the local Resonance.<br /> <br /> A Master of Spirit can temporarily destroy the Gauntlet in an area despite the Gauntlet being typically omnipresent between worlds.<br /> <br /> There is no reason for a Master of Fate not to be able to call up something as fleeting as a Hedge gate that is not founded in the Changeling fandom's ongoing beef with Mage: the Awakening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages can do a lot of things, but on the other hand, they can't do everything either if there's a powerful magic force telling them no. </div> </div> </div>And the Hedge is not maintained by a powerful magic force of the sort that directly gives a shit about the comings and goings of its visitors. This isn't God-Machine anti-tampering measures stopping angels from being directly compelled to Fall, this is &quot;there may or may not still be a by-crossing-this-threshold-you-agree-to-the-terms-and-conditions clause attached to the use of a Hedge gate from the mortal world, and a Master of Fate has the ability to meddle with the terms of supernatural agreements.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T12:55:19-07:00","id":1070812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1067420#post1067420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1e had a fairly extensive list that can be summarized as &quot;things in the Hedge are affected by the Arcana that they appear to be (living things with Life, inanimate objects with Matter, etc) unless they're part of the Thorns,&quot; &quot;sensory magic has its dicepool capped by your Wisdom rating,&quot; and &quot;you cannot exit the Hedge except through a Hedge gate.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2e shifts some of this \u2014 Hedge Gates are subject to the same rules as other Irises, for instance, so a Master of Fate can leave the Hedge as readily as a Master of Death can escape the Underworld \u2014 but more detailed information will likely show up in the Crossover Chronicle eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ....I...think I agree with you? However....Mage pg. 133.<br /> <br /> &quot;Open Avernian Gate (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Making<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Crafts, Persuasion<br /> The mage rips open the material world to the Underworld,<br /> creating an Iris between the material world and the upper layers<br /> of the Underworld within the area of effect. Opening the gate<br /> causes the area to gain a Death Resonance and the Gateway<br /> Condition for the Duration of the spell.<br /> +1 Reach: The mage can create an Iris leading to anywhere<br /> she has been before in the Underworld.&quot;<br /> <br /> So by my reading, you are correct. Technically. A Master of Fate would have no more luck forming an exit OUT of the Hedge than a Master of Death could form a portal out of the underworld. Since this spell only describe a Mage &quot;ripping open the material world to the Underworld&quot; e.g.- standing in the mundane world and invoking magic to form a gate into the underworld my assumption is that trying to do the same from the opposite side is impossible. You can use the gate you already created, for sure, and you can probably extend the duration of the condition to near indefinite. I'll even speculate that a Mage can probably open any portal to the surface he finds without needing a proper key. But he can't snap his fingers and get a fresh exit. He needs to have one already on hand, including a gate he brought into being with the above spell and a little Reach that placed in at a depth usually not found in the underworld. <br /> <br /> I think we can be a little more generous with the Hedge. It generally wants its victims to stay, but its more forgiving and playful than the realm of the dead about the ones who want to get out. So... 1.) Any mage of fate can form a hedge gate from the material world into the Hedge without trouble. With a little extra Reach you can go anywhere you've ever been inside the Hedge....if the place still exists. Keep in mind, the Hedge is amorphous and ever changing, so you might want to pick a locale that has some staying power like a goblin market, a goblin village, a fae hollow, or one of those other rare places that resist alteration. 2.) A mage can easily form a way OUT of the Hedge near the mortal realm, just like a changeling. Such gates might have their own quirks- like thenceforth being openable from either side by such entities like the fae who are capable of opening a &quot;natural&quot; gate into the hedge. 3.) A Mage can open a pre-existing gateway out of the hedge anywhere within the hedge, including one he created by magic in the mortal world. 4.) If a Mage is lost or deep enough within the Hedge, he cannot create a gateway out of the hedge until he finds his way back to a path that brushes against the mortal world, as per rule number 2. <br /> <br /> While I agree Mages are and rightfully should be considered exceptionally powerful in Second Edition compared to other supernatural beings, I believe the scope of their abilities has been somewhat misinterpreted, especially when it comes to Realms beyond this Earth. I'll also be the first to admit that I haven't read Mage as completely as I have other Chronicles of Darkness, so if there is written material that calls my own interpretation into question please feel free to bring it up. I'd just ask for relevant page numbers and source material for ease of reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T13:24:38-07:00","id":1070825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1070812#post1070812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So by my reading, you are correct. Technically. A Master of Fate would have no more luck forming an exit OUT of the Hedge than a Master of Death could form a portal out of the underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>The tricky part is that we haven't got much direct information on how the Underworld works in 2e's mechanics besides a couple tidbits in the Demon Storyteller's Guide, which takes liberties for expediency on other subjects (e.g. Prometheans having innate 3/3 Armor) and only mentions applying a penalty roughly equivalent to a Withstand rating of 1 to attempts by non-Sin-Eaters to leave; there's no special consideration mentioned in Mage's brief writeup of the Underworld, those being limited to the place's leniency of Paradox with regards to Death spells and its impact on living visitors' Virtue and Vice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll even speculate that a Mage can probably open any portal to the surface he finds without needing a proper key. </div> </div> </div>That is, in fact, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/872952-a-changeling-related-question?p=873580#post873580\">a regular Death Weaving effect</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T13:26:00-07:00","id":1070826,"title":"","content":"I don't think the spell should be read as only being able to create an Avernian Gate from the material. It's just that the writer assumed it would be created while in the material because being in the material is default for almost all mages.<br /> Besides, Dave Brookshaw wrote in that post linked earlier that it was completely possible to create a Hedge Gate while inside the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T15:09:53-07:00","id":1070876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1070826#post1070826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the spell should be read as only being able to create an Avernian Gate from the material. It's just that the writer assumed it would be created while in the material because being in the material is default for almost all mages.<br /> Besides, Dave Brookshaw wrote in that post linked earlier that it was completely possible to create a Hedge Gate while inside the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Shrug. Not really disputing whether or not a Mage CAN create a hedge gate. Just where and when. And most of all, how easy it should be under a given circumstance. I mean, even on Earth magic gets harder depending on how obvious and how many witnesses there are. The Hedge cares nothing for who sees you. But it has RULES, sir! One does not just LEAVE before their part is played! Turning back at the threshold is fine, of course, plenty of sisters and brothers of the poor hero have done that. No harm, no foul. But for those who choose to go further in its not proper at all. They've become COMMITTED. Now there's a tale to tell, and no tale simply STOPS until it has a proper ENDING. Does a prince show himself and fail to remove the curse with a kiss? What sort of wolf would learn of a tasty creature living in a certain house and fail to enact a plot to invade the home? No no no. There are traditions and patterns and rules and if you disagree you will surely be PUNISHED. <br /> <br /> Which is a long winded way of saying that a Mage deep in the Hedge should, by my reading, have at best a hefty set of penalties on the dice for getting back out. If he no longer has a good grasp on where the mortal world is relative to himself (which of course happens all the damn time in the Hedge) it gets worse. The easy way to mitigate the problem would be to find your way back (and probably suffer through some strange encounter arranged by the Wyrd along the way). Another way might to fulfill some barely understandable purpose between you and the Wyrd (&quot;Why yes, Mr. Hobgoblin, I am a learned sorcerer and can answer your obscure question!&quot;...and hopefully Mr. Hobgoblin doesn't use the knowledge you gave him to sneak into the mortal world and devour your sister's son...the Wyrd is a bitch that way) and then invoke your magic. But as a general rule, the deeper you go the harder you will find escape, but there might be ways to get around that problem if you fulfill the demands of Fate and the Wyrd (which is really just Fate when it gets bored and a little drunk). <br /> <br /> Also, if you do manage to push your way past Fate's designs and create your door, might want to be careful anyway. Yeah, maybe it'll lead to your inner sanctum as planned, but Fate might have worked its way into the enchantment more than you knew and you could end up falling 100 stories to your death or find yourself staring at a pack of Abyssal dogs on the hunt for mana to suck from a mage's bones. Or maybe Fate is cowed by your mastery but whispers to its good freind Time and you end up a few centuries beyond the mark. <br /> <br /> Before we get completely off topic for my whimsy, I'll throw in a few more questions I kind of allude to here. How much control does a Mage generally have over his destination with these Irises? Are there any factors that can fuck with that control, ala how lost they are, what forces in the universe might be opposing them, etc. How long does the portal stay open, and how many things can come through besides the mage (hell, could a swiftly moving hobgoblin or desperate changeling get the drop on a Mage and skip on through his portal before he can, perhaps with the damn gate shutting in the Mage's face?). Given the rules the Hedge normally plays by, does the gate eventually vanish as the Avernian Gate does in the referenced spell....or does it stay in place forever waiting to be reopened?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T15:18:00-07:00","id":1070883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1070747#post1070747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also not the kind of oath that a mage is going to know about casually</div> </div> </div> </div> Its simplicity within itself for an Acanthus get an Informed Condition through magic to tell you about a Freehold or Court Oaths. The smallest amount of research at any point of time WILL know about that casually. Its such a major part of changeling lore that not learning it is strange. Even if not, its even simpler to mass change every pledge (sealing, oath, bargain and vow) on the ling at once. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Hedge is not <i>that </i>special and it is actively detrimental to Changeling's presentation to try to make it so considering how much space 1e already wasted on playing up the Arcadia Problem. </div> </div> </div> Yes, it is that special, because becoming Lost in the Hedge is supposed to be a real danger. Its the theme of the Thorns. This is a unique feature of the Hedge that no other realm has specifically because <br /> <br /> It has nothing to do with trying to deal with mages and everything to do with maintaining the story of the Hedge. If you want to change that for your game, feel free. But its not what we have precidence and story for, and no real reason to change the established rule, and every reason to leave it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T15:42:14-07:00","id":1070893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1070883#post1070883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Its simplicity within itself for an Acanthus get an Informed Condition through magic to tell you about a Freehold or Court Oaths. The smallest amount of research at any point of time WILL know about that casually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowing that changeling freeholds and Courts exist is not the same as knowing the affiliations of a specific changeling, the Informed Condition does not represent specific concrete information in itself, and &quot;the smallest amount of research&quot; doesn't help when the species' default specialty Safe Place <i>makes finding out about its residents harder to accomplish</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its such a major part of changeling lore that not learning it is strange. Even if not, its even simpler to mass change every pledge (sealing, oath, bargain and vow) on the ling at once. </div> </div> </div>Sever Oaths is Duration-primary and Withstood by Composure and changelings have Composure as one of their most important Attributes due to the nature of breaking points. Just changing one Oath on a changeling with a not-unexpected Composure rating of 3 already reduces the base dicepool of an Adept to raw Gnosis.<br /> <br /> Step out of the hyperabstracted nightmare scenario: How much groundwork are you discounting in the name of this complaint? How much of what we know about how supernatural societies tend to work are you shortcutting past for the sake of argument? Where is this hypothetical actually coming from? Because it's certainly <i>theoretically possible</i> for a single mage to rewrite the oaths of an <i>entire freehold</i> in one casting, but given the number of failure points that exist along the way to altering the bonds of just one of the fae that's something you build a whole story around, because <i>How did it get this far?</i> is a question you don't get to skip over in the name of a mechanical complaint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, it is that special, because becoming Lost in the Hedge is supposed to be a real danger. </div> </div> </div>And it <i>is</i>. Mastery of Fate is not something you reach casually. Masters are not commonplace.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It has nothing to do with trying to deal with mages and everything to do with maintaining the story of the Hedge. </div> </div> </div>The story of the Hedge is that it's a place that's easy to fall into and difficult to get out of for the vast majority of people. Changelings being able to use their connection to the force of destiny presided over by the Wyrd to shape a path at extreme levels of power is not meaningfully different from a mage that has spent time and effort learning the secrets of Fate to the limits of mortal Awakened being able to use the strongest variety of spell at their disposal to override an otherwise-common limitation of the realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T16:10:32-07:00","id":1070909,"title":"","content":"&quot;Knowing that changeling freeholds and Courts exist is not the same as knowing the affiliations of a specific changeling, the Informed Condition does not represent specific concrete information in itself, and &quot;the smallest amount of research&quot; doesn't help when the species' default specialty Safe Place <i>makes finding out about its residents harder to accomplish</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Missed this detail in second edition. Does whatever this penalty is apply to mundane efforts to find them as well? I was aware the true fae had challenges to go through, but not everyone else...<br /> <br /> &quot;Sever Oaths is Duration-primary and Withstood by Composure and changelings have Composure as one of their most important Attributes due to the nature of breaking points. Just changing one Oath on a changeling with a not-unexpected Composure rating of 3 already reduces the base dicepool of an Adept to raw Gnosis.&quot;<br /> <br /> See, this is the part I don't get. It makes sense if you managed to cancel out a contract that it would eventually come back. Maybe I'm just used to 1st edition, but to me if a normal oath of any sort gets &quot;severed&quot; it implies a permanent loss, as if the terms of the oath were violated and the changeling cannot gain access to them unless they seek out a new agreement with the same parties. Having to know the ins and outs and wording of the entire oath seems like a much much weaker spell than level 4 would imply.<br /> <br /> &quot;Step out of the hyperabstracted nightmare scenario: How much groundwork are you discounting in the name of this complaint? How much of what we know about how supernatural societies tend to work are you shortcutting past for the sake of argument? Where is this hypothetical actually coming from? Because it's certainly <i>theoretically possible</i> for a single mage to rewrite the oaths of an <i>entire freehold</i> in one casting, but given the number of failure points that exist along the way to altering the bonds of just one of the fae that's something you build a whole story around, because <i>How did it get this far?</i> is a question you don't get to skip over in the name of a mechanical complaint.&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, the foundations of fae society are absolutely much more heavily on magical oaths than basically any other supernatural group, with the arguable exception of Demons and the way their whole facade of existence depends on who's souls they have managed to slurp up. And while I'll give you that the spell is fairly useless against the fae if you have to learn as much of the oath as you are suggesting, my reading of it implied that the mage could just snap a finger and BOOM you are no longer a member of the equivalent to the Adamantine Arrow or worse that Mage society in general forget you were a part of it....AND now the abyss and/or the Exarchs have a much easier time of finding you if they are on the hunt. Kill the right oath and that's exactly what would happen to a Changeling. Their whole society is THAT rooted in their bargains.<br /> <br /> &quot;And it <i>is</i>. Mastery of Fate is not something you reach casually. Masters are not commonplace.&quot;<br /> <br /> Okay, yes. But even the most powerful heroes of legend who entered the underworld or the realms of the fae had long journeys and did not make it back out easily. I mean....there are GODS in these stories that have a harder time dealing with these other realms than your suggesting Mages have. I have trouble getting behind this view of reducing the other realms to mere vacation spots for an accomplished Dr. Strange. <br /> <br /> &quot;The story of the Hedge is that it's a place that's easy to fall into and difficult to get out of for the vast majority of people. Changelings being able to use their connection to the force of destiny presided over by the Wyrd to shape a path at extreme levels of power is not meaningfully different from a mage that has spent time and effort learning the secrets of Fate to the limits of mortal Awakened being able to use the strongest variety of spell at their disposal to override an otherwise-common limitation of the realm.&quot;<br /> <br /> And making a path through the Hedge still sounds more dangerous than calling up an exit anywhere you want. Also, a powerful changeling would still need to have a sense of direction (if your lost and don't know where you are going, being able to form a path is kind of useless). A Mage who is also lost would, from what you seem to be telling us, still be able to call up his insta-exit without trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T17:35:30-07:00","id":1070949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1070909#post1070909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Missed this detail in second edition. Does whatever this penalty is apply to mundane efforts to find them as well? I was aware the true fae had challenges to go through, but not everyone else...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;While a changeling is inside her Hollow, the Merit's rating [to a limit of 5] is subtracted from any attempts to learn her personal information, as if she had the Anonymity Merit at an equal rating. Attempts to pursue or track her, both supernatural and mundane, are hindered by the same penalty.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See, this is the part I don't get. It makes sense if you managed to cancel out a contract that it would eventually come back. Maybe I'm just used to 1st edition, but to me if a normal oath of any sort gets &quot;severed&quot; it implies a permanent loss, as if the terms of the oath were violated and the changeling cannot gain access to them unless they seek out a new agreement with the same parties. Having to know the ins and outs and wording of the entire oath seems like a much much weaker spell than level 4 would imply. </div> </div> </div>The spell has multiple potential effects, the relevant one of which is &quot;Modify or negate an oath or other supernatural agreement reinforced by the dictates of Fate,&quot; and is one of two core spells in the Fate Arcanum that deal with Awakened oathbinding in more than a sensory capacity (the other being Sworn Oaths); the other effects the spell can accomplish include changing how a given oath's bonuses or penalties manifest, altering or removing a spell's conditional trigger, releasing bound souls and ephemeral beings, or rewriting a Destiny-bearing subject's Doom.<br /> <br /> All of these effects need the full extent of a Master's free Reach to be made Lasting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And while I'll give you that the spell is fairly useless against the fae if you have to learn as much of the oath as you are suggesting, my reading of it implied that the mage could just snap a finger and BOOM you are no longer a member of the equivalent to the Adamantine Arrow or worse that Mage society in general forget you were a part of it....AND now the abyss and/or the Exarchs have a much easier time of finding you if they are on the hunt. Kill the right oath and that's exactly what would happen to a Changeling. Their whole society is THAT rooted in their bargains. </div> </div> </div>As a general note, part of the reason I have so little patience for the &quot;mages are broken&quot; arguments is that they all exist a very short distance away from the white room nonsense where &quot;just snap a finger and BOOM&quot; is how things actually play out.<br /> <br /> Mage society is assembled through Status Merits and partially reinforced through oathbinding of the same sort that Sever Oaths is primarily written to handle. Somehow the existence of the Acanthus does not cause this arrangement to implode despite the greater likelihood for mages that know each other to have grievances, possibly because the primary use of the spell we're talking about is to <i>let someone get out of an unwanted oath</i>, not to casually dick around with a party for no stated reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, yes. But even the most powerful heroes of legend who entered the underworld or the realms of the fae had long journeys and did not make it back out easily. I mean....there are GODS in these stories that have a harder time dealing with these other realms than your suggesting Mages have. I have trouble getting behind this view of reducing the other realms to mere vacation spots for an accomplished Dr. Strange. </div> </div> </div>These characters need a minimum Gnosis of 5 to have Mastery in just the one Arcanum. By that point the things within their capability technically include the power to sustain a small ecosystem. They have the unique ability among their fellows to develop mnemonic shortcuts that lesser mages can use to aid their spellcraft even before getting into Arcanum-specific things like pocket realms and wholesale creation of life \u2014 they're the mage equivalent of ephemeral beings with the Mass Create Influence without the innate durability of born monsters. Many of them are sufficiently paranoid that they seldom leave their Sanctums unless they have to, whether that be because their obsessions have driven them to do things that offended the gods or because they're acting as the keystone for too many projects or simply because they figure (sometimes not incorrectly) that reality is out to get them.<br /> <br /> It's not much of a vacation when you still have to abide by diplomacy \u2014 the corollary of &quot;spellcasting works best with time and quiet&quot; is &quot;spellcasting is fucked when things go wrong,&quot; and so many things can go wrong in the Underworld or the Hedge even if you do have a pocket escape route, whether that be because every Dominion of the Great Below is presided over by a hostile deity or because looking for trouble in the fae borderlands is literally asking for trouble it's only too prepared to give.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And making a path through the Hedge still sounds more dangerous than calling up an exit anywhere you want. </div> </div> </div>Making a path through the Hedge means you are inherently out of the most dangerous part of the Hedge short of the gates of Faerie themselves \u2014 the Thorns are a legitimate obstacle to navigation.<br /> <br /> Even with the limitation imposed in 1e, there was nothing stopping you from teleporting <i>to</i> a gate-viable feature with sufficient mastery of the Space Arcanum, and the abstracted nature of distance within the Hedge means even below the level of ability needed outright forge an exit you still have the capacity to <i>twist luck to help you find a suitable portal</i>.<br /> <br /> This is to say nothing of how leaving the Hedge is demonstrably less of a quicksand-pit than it was in 1e \u2014 there's a hard interval on how long it takes to look for an exit based on environment rather than a time-based interval that gets worse the longer you look.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, a powerful changeling would still need to have a sense of direction (if your lost and don't know where you are going, being able to form a path is kind of useless). A Mage who is also lost would, from what you seem to be telling us, still be able to call up his insta-exit without trouble. </div> </div> </div>Unless the mage in question is also an Adept of Time, their ability to form a gate without risk of Paradox is limited to either making an instantaneous portal that lasts for up to thirty seconds (and losing Sympathy to the place thereafter) or taking half an hour of ritual to make one that can last for at least a scene without getting into penalties.<br /> <br /> How many powerful changelings do you imagine <i>survive</i> without a sense of direction? How do you think navigating <i>a place that throws obstacles in front of you based on where you're trying to go</i> works?<br /> <br /> This is one of the most malleable otherworlds in the setting responding to a level of magic that can <i>create borderline impossible circumstances</i> as a function of its influence over fate and destiny. &quot;Make a Hedge gate&quot; is <i>tame</i> compared to the sort of things Making and Unmaking spells can accomplish \u2014 and the consequences of careless use of Awakened magic are sufficiently universal that being in a place that <i>erodes your ability to safely contain your powers</i> isn't something most Masters are going to undertake lightly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T21:27:32-07:00","id":1071028,"title":"","content":"This seems like a REALLY heated topic so I dunno if I can pick it apart in a short span of time, but maybe I can offer a compromise to the central topic---a topic I think is also in the wrong forum to begin with but whatever!<br /> <br /> So to begin with, I appreciate Dave's input but the 1e Changeling books <i>did</i> want even Mages to be held to the laws of the Hedge. Maybe that is shifting a bit, but I think that both can be right.<br /> <br /> A Master of Fate <i>can</i> make a Hedge Gate. But doing so will still violate a Contract. The Mage is under Contract, knowingly or not, to exit the Hedge legally. If they break that Contract, their life is going to get more interesting very quickly. Maybe not everyone will enjoy this sort of &quot;fix&quot; I'm proposing, but I think it is a fair one considering that 1E mage had realms that Masters of Space cannot escape from <i>either.</i><br /> Namely the Crossways.<br /> <br /> So anyone who wants Mages to be able to make irises in and out of the Hedge without Archmastery are going to be breaking the Contract that they implicitly agree to when they enter the Hedge. Consent is not a part of this contract at any time.<br /> <br /> The other thing I wanna mention is something I think Satchel is trying to say too. Mages are arrogant bastards that trample all over the cosmos. Yes, that's their sthick. If you don't like it, deal with it. And by deal with it, have an ST who looooves hubris. What I'm actually saying is, you don't need paradox to bring about a Mage's hubris. Any mage player who is really good can probably evade any of the punishments they have coming their way but it will come at the cost of some of their freedom and peace-of-mind. Logically this is how hermit-mages come to be. They've pissed off so many forces-of-nature that they can't go anywhere without it being open season. If a Mage <i>can</i> do anything, it will have consequences. It doesn't have to be easy.<br /> <br /> With that said, I do prefer the idea that the Hedge can fight back against a Mage. Fate 5 Gateway out of the Hedge? Sure, but here's a clash of wills you gotta pass against a being you cannot see, possibly the Hedge itself. Prooobably won't pass it, but maybe you'll get lucky. That's what Fate's for right?<br /> <br /> Maybe Mage magic can deal with the thorns, but maybe the Thorns have a Withstand you're just not going to get through without an exceptional success. If they do succeed, maybe some other form of ire will follow them.<br /> <br /> Any punishment or vengeful response the forces of Faerie might throw at the mage might also be something the Mage has a counter for, but in the end they've created an endless chess-game of consequences for themselves all because they broke the Contracts of the Hedge.<br /> <br /> There'd be no easy fix for that short of Archmastery and a whole lot of deal-making.<br /> <br /> And all that would have been prevented if the arrogant Mage hadn't broken the Contract, which they'll know better if they're listening to their mentors or listening to changeling's for half a second.<br /> <br /> And while all of that could just seem annoying to a mage player, or as a half-assed &quot;fix&quot; to changeling players, from a Storyteller perspective I think it sounds <i>interesting.</i><br /> <br /> Kind of like a Breaking Bad thing where its just one problem after another because of 1 really dumb life-choice. You could build an entire story off of this single choice to break the Hedge's rules. It could be especially interesting if it ends up being that the only ones with the social clout to get the Mage out of this endless chess-game is swallowing their pride and asking changelings for help or guidance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T21:55:04-07:00","id":1071042,"title":"","content":"Oh, another thread that devolved into 1) theoretical mages theoretically being the most powerful being ever, 2) internal consistency of mages' cosmology being mistaken for external consistency, and 3) the magical equivalent of saying that anyone with a gun can trivially murder the President of (insert country) with just a single shot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T00:01:03-07:00","id":1071101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1071028#post1071028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Master of Fate <i>can</i> make a Hedge Gate. But doing so will still violate a Contract. The Mage is under Contract, knowingly or not, to exit the Hedge legally. If they break that Contract, their life is going to get more interesting very quickly. Maybe not everyone will enjoy this sort of &quot;fix&quot; I'm proposing, but I think it is a fair one considering that 1E mage had realms that Masters of Space cannot escape from <i>either.</i><br /> Namely the Crossways.<br /> <br /> So anyone who wants Mages to be able to make irises in and out of the Hedge without Archmastery are going to be breaking the Contract that they implicitly agree to when they enter the Hedge. Consent is not a part of this contract at any time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like that idea, particularly since it also applies to why Demons can use Rip The Gates to get into the Hedge, but they can't use it to get back out again. I've taken the God-Machine and the Hedg to being like two different computer systems; the hardware and operating systems are somewhat similar, but programs that are technically compatible between them are going to have features that don't work right because they're looking for resources that either don't exist or are different from what's required. Different laws, different overbearing entities that warp and somewhat control the populace to particular designs.<br /> <br /> Sorry, that was off topic, but I do feel your post sums up both the problem and the solution rather nicely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T11:53:14-07:00","id":1071355,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7967\" data-vbnamecard=\"7967\">Scarlet Witch</a> That's a good suggestion and a good analysis, and it ulitmately comes down to ST policing and bedeviling their players. I've met some, not a whole lot but not a small sample either, of players that just want the power trip and ignore the consequences. Which is where the whole tension comes from.<br /> <br /> Now to the broader topic. we do have two tools in the system to mediate these conflicting precedents. Withstand and Clash of Wills. These two can help make a gradual easy to difficult scaling and availability. Public access areas are generally not as protected or guarded as VIP areas. and certainly it's no cakewalk for changelings escaping the first time around.<br /> <br /> My idea is merely a suggestion. But others in the thread have pointed out extensively and to length about the required system mastery and in game legwork to get this kind of thing off the ground. So whether the suggestion is another add powerstat and resistance to withstand, and thus unneeded, I'm not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T21:44:57-07:00","id":1071608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1071028#post1071028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Master of Fate <i>can</i> make a Hedge Gate. But doing so will still violate a Contract. The Mage is under Contract, knowingly or not, to exit the Hedge legally. If they break that Contract, their life is going to get more interesting very quickly. Maybe not everyone will enjoy this sort of &quot;fix&quot; I'm proposing, but I think it is a fair one considering that 1E mage had realms that Masters of Space cannot escape from <i>either.</i><br /> Namely the Crossways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the problem, expressed in terms of its separate elements:<br /> <br /> The Crossways is an Abyssal incursion specifically built around victims getting stuck deeper and deeper inside a maddening spiral of unreality, as a thing specifically and primarily extant to bedevil and/or entrap mages, sometimes as a direct result of their carelessness with magic. There's one way in and out per manifestation and Space needs the support of an extra Arcanum to reach outside of its bounds for communication. The Abyss has business directly negating easy shortcuts past core problems it presents to mages, because it's as omnipresent as the Supernal is and serves as one of the central pillars of how Phenomenal reality feels oppressive to the practice of Awakened magic.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is an ever-shifting combination of elven thoroughfare and fateful borderland nestled around the physical/metaphorical space where dreams happen, and its entrances and exits \u2014 of which there are many \u2014 regularly possess keys of no more substantial difficulty to use than those of any of the other run-of-the-mill Irises the Awakened encounter. People can and do get out of the Hedge on purpose or by luck, and the former category includes people who are fairies who can brute-force the creation of an exit with a suitable (and, in 2e's presentation, visually unique rather than archetypal) door/archway/mirror/threshold; in other words, if there <i>is</i> an agreement, it's one that's flexible enough that a legal gateway is relatively easy to finagle for anyone with the right &quot;in&quot; with fate even if you don't have the capacity to trick a gate into opening by faking its key.<br /> <br /> The Arcana of Awakened magic are increasingly capable of things that just plain shouldn't work according to the common sense of their respective portions of reality \u2014 Matter can make steel a liquid at room temperature, Prime can make tass that doesn't have any Mana in it, Spirit can transform you into a Twilight state even in realms where Twilight isn't a state that exists, Death can make a ghost possess its body for a lot longer than the scene/hour it would normally be able to maintain that Manifestation, and so on and so forth. Of particular note here is that at the level of proficiency in Fate immediately below the one needed to make a Hedge gate, you literally have the ability to alter the terms of a supernatural agreement enforced by the dictates of fate, and <i>at</i> that level, you can accomplish things like a spontaneous solar eclipse or a normal human going skydiving without a parachute and surviving.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, the setting's attitude toward crossover is such that the various cosmic-level forces that concern themselves mostly with singular gamelines aren't too worried about individual attempts at skirting their territory \u2014 the God-Machine stops wholesale subversion of Its angels because It is a precision-oriented process and an angel breaking its defining orders of &quot;do not betray your mission&quot; has severe consequences beyond the immediate scope of whatever it is made to do instead, and a Fae Prop created to perform a specific task can only be stopped from performing that specific task by another act of god, but Luna's hands-off approach to Her children and the Divine Fire's questionable presence of mind in general tend to be the norm \u2014 things like the Judges and the Exarchs are where you get the kind of direct possessive behavior for things on a smaller scale than violating the sanctity of a phenomenon's metaphysical makeup/affiliation; everybody else, especially the older and more jaded among the Fae, doesn't really <i>care</i>.<br /> <br /> All of which is to say that the pettiest circumstances the Wyrd gets involved with concern the keeping to the letter of one's word, and even in 1e Changeling included elements that dealt with getting around the spirit of a vow's original context; an unspoken agreement like the one implied to be behind the forbiddance in 1e is no agreement at all, particularly when creating an exit is still <i>using</i> an exit and even in 1e the capacity existed to fake a key to open a gate. There's basically no coherent means of outright blocking the ability that wouldn't arbitrarily disregard a lot of things about both gamelines.<br /> <br /> If you absolutely must add more difficulty to the process, I wouldn't go with blanket immunity. No, take cues from Goetic Summons and the intervals for finding an active gateway \u2014 add one Reach to open a gateway from a region of the Hedge corresponding to a less populated area, or two Reach from mostly uninhabited wilderness, with denser spaces being accessible with the default parameters of the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-01-2017, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T23:41:31-07:00","id":1071634,"title":"","content":"Yikes, I can't tell if you're irritated with me or not... That was a lot to say for a technicality over the definition of &quot;exit.&quot; I am actually still not convinced, just because your example describes how changelings can make entrances. The Hedge doesn't care how you get it, it cares how you get out. Mages are not Fae, so I don't think they have permission to leave more easily than fae could. If we're going to be talking about the big name metaphysics of the games, I'll just say again that I prefer keeping into the spirit of mage's theme of hubris and that, for the Hedge in particular, it is not the cakewalk they'd expect it to be. As dangerous as the Underworld is, it is, and probably should be, more hospitable than the Hedge.<br /> <br /> I will hope you did notice I didn't forcefully argue for blanket immunity though, I just wanted a bunch of possible ways of making it more difficult that would fit people's tastes, and make it difficult not for balance, or fairness, or whatever, but because a Mage's life is more exciting if it has <i>consequences.</i> If I can get away with whatever I want, especially because I'm an Acanthus, then my ST isn't doing their job!<br /> <br /> As a player, I would expect, and anticipate, the Hedge to be more dangerous by virtue of its nature than the Underworld or the Shadow. The greater difficulty of how to get back out safely makes it more <i>exciting.</i> At least for me it does. And that's why I argue for my case. These games are games, yes, but they're storyteller games, so they're here for us to make interesting stories. If your story requires mages to get in and out of the hedge without muss-or-fuss then so be it? Cuz the rules are not as important as a cool game dripping with atmosphere. But for me, the atmosphere is dripping if the Hedge is dangerous enough that no mage <i>dares</i> go in without supplies, an escape plan, and a heart beating with fear and anticipation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T04:00:17-07:00","id":1071673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1071634#post1071634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will hope you did notice I didn't forcefully argue for blanket immunity though, I just wanted a bunch of possible ways of making it more difficult that would fit people's tastes, and make it difficult not for balance, or fairness, or whatever, but because a Mage's life is more exciting if it has <i>consequences.</i> If I can get away with whatever I want, especially because I'm an Acanthus, then my ST isn't doing their job!</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the main consequence I see from the rules as written is Fate Masters going &quot;I can come and leave whenever I wish! Why should I worry about the consequences?&quot;<br /> Which is EXACTLY in line with the themes of Mage. Hubris and arrogance giving Mages more than enough rope to hang themselves with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T22:57:09-07:00","id":1071929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1071673#post1071673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, the main consequence I see from the rules as written is Fate Masters going &quot;I can come and leave whenever I wish! Why should I worry about the consequences?&quot;<br /> Which is EXACTLY in line with the themes of Mage. Hubris and arrogance giving Mages more than enough rope to hang themselves with.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can't be a world of darkness without a whole lot of danger :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T23:28:09-07:00","id":1071936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1071929#post1071929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It can't be a world of darkness without a whole lot of danger :3</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. Actually, surprisingly, it can. In fact, it's ability to be thus is a fairly large part of Changeling's makeup. I mean, not all games should not have a majority of not danger, not even within Changeling, but part of Changeling's strength relies on the non-dangery bits, such that you really could carry it on that.<br /> <br /> I mean, some of that depends on how you define danger I suppose, but the Chronicles of Darkness can be dark without danger in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T04:08:55-07:00","id":1071975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1071673#post1071673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, the main consequence I see from the rules as written is Fate Masters going &quot;I can come and leave whenever I wish! Why should I worry about the consequences?&quot;<br /> Which is EXACTLY in line with the themes of Mage. Hubris and arrogance giving Mages more than enough rope to hang themselves with.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah, but the problem is that Mage themes shouldn't ignore the themes of Changeling either. Why should Mage's themes ignore Changeling's? Or should Awakened magic be able to ignore rules more than a Demon's?<br /> <br /> As I said before, in 1e, no one could open a gateway out of the Hedge. Not changelings, not the Gentry, not the goblins. In 1e was described as a massive Contract (or other form of pledge magic) with the Hedge itself. And there's lines in 2e that suggest that this is still true. &quot;The Lost can enter the Hedge through any door in the human world. They must leave through established entrances and exits, though.&quot; And we have: &quot;There aren\u2019t a lot of hard rules in the Hedge. But these few things are always true: \u2022 It\u2019s always easy to get lost in the Hedge.&quot; And that rule applies to Gentry, Huntsmen, goblin, changeling, mortal and others alike. <br /> <br /> A mage could, in theory, open a gate, but they'd have to beat a Clash of Wills against the god-level being who's established that Contract in the Hedge, and good luck with that. We have precident for this kind of thing as well (re: altering angels). Now, that might have changed in 2e, and its very possible it has. But until we see something to that effect, I'm going to go with the hints we've seen in Changeling and Demon (re: Rip the Gates).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T15:49:20-07:00","id":1072223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1071975#post1071975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ah, but the problem is that Mage themes shouldn't ignore the themes of Changeling either. Why should Mage's themes ignore Changeling's? Or should Awakened magic be able to ignore rules more than a Demon's?</div> </div> </div> </div>Awakened magic is very specifically themed around ignoring more and more significant rules with greater mastery of the Arcana \u2014 again, by Fate 5 you have the ability to make substantially more improbable things happen than the appearance of another hole in the colander on top of being able to twist a loophole into any mystical bargain you can get your head around and having the ability to Clash any attempt to fetter your will.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Hedge keeps hold of the vast majority of the people that find themselves within it unless they have supernatural aid&quot; is both not a theme of Changeling in any meaningful sense and not actually contradicted by &quot;The Hedge can be induced to open a gateway to the mortal world by one of the most powerful forms of supernatural aid available to characters that the system normally bothers to represent with game statistics.&quot;<br /> <br /> Demon's &quot;rule-breaking&quot; powers work on weird lateral applications of the principles that angels use, which themselves manage to be applied to material reality by demons without Clashing with the Machine on every other use. It's not a comparable phenomenon to meddling with the volatile fundament of reality itself to temporarily make the improbable happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I said before, in 1e, no one could open a gateway out of the Hedge. Not changelings, not the Gentry, not the goblins. </div> </div> </div>1e had tokens that enabled outright direct travel to or from Arcadia. The primary means of getting them was to trade one from a Stranger.<br /> <br /> 1e had Hedge gates that consisted of rituals that worked in very broad swathes of location, as well as trods between Earth and Faerie that were both wide and short.<br /> <br /> 1e made a point of specifying both that the Gentry always knew where They were going and that the Wyrd contrived circumstances that enabled Them to play out Their Legends.<br /> <br /> 1e and 2e both have made it plain that several goblins and other contents of the Hedge don't leave because they cannot exist outside of it.<br /> <br /> 1e's stipulation was that you had to use a gateway to get out of the Hedge and could not simply teleport out with Space alone; this is not a limitation unique to the Hedge, and the spell under discussion does involve using a gateway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A mage could, in theory, open a gate, but they'd have to beat a Clash of Wills against the god-level being who's established that Contract in the Hedge, and good luck with that. We have precident for this kind of thing as well (re: altering angels). </div> </div> </div>Again: compelling an angel to forsake its mission has consequences that do not exist for allowing the most powerful variety of mage short of an archmaster to affect entry or egress to or from the Hedge. Nothing about being able to get out of the Hedge inherently disrupts a godlike being's intricate ten-thousand-step plan and reforges a lesser divinity into a rogue agent.<br /> <br /> This is to say nothing of how you're interpreting &quot;entering the Hedge is an oath&quot; as &quot;a discrete godlike being swore an oath with the Hedge to make it inescapable and cares if somebody does like fairies do to get around it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Consider: a character who can freely open a portal into or out of the Hedge affects the setting by their inclusion if they make use of that ability in a manner that traces back to the larger narrative of a chronicle. What does the freehold do if they hear of multiple accounts of Lost getting out from deep within the Thorns after an encounter with a mysterious figure? What about the motley who takes in a stranger and finds their Hollow door opening to a place none of them have ever been? What about the privateer who witnesses a small household thrown upon the briarwolves' mercy after offending their surprise dinner guest? What about the influx of otherworldly visitors brought to Earth by the tit-for-tat nature of the Hedge interacting strangely with the sudden hiccup in the number of gateways in a region? What about the newly-posted job offer/bounty at the goblin market for a wyrd-twisting willworker as broker/barker/slave? What about the Stranger who's had their interest piqued by the activities of a fate-shaper who isn't protected by the Bulwark? How do you attempt to deal with any of that?<br /> <br /> Masters have access to powers on the lower end of plot-device level, and as mages they tend to conduct themselves with an according level of care or severely disrupt the natural order of their surroundings until they get a hold of themselves or self-destruct in the course of impatience and/or overextension. Their ability to circumvent the normal strictures of the Hedge no more ruins Changeling for their interaction than a Master of Spirit's ability to create a Place-That-Isn't ruins Werewolf crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-02-2017, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T16:04:25-07:00","id":1072229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1072223#post1072223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awakened magic is very specifically themed around ignoring more and more significant rules with greater mastery of the Arcana</div> </div> </div> </div> If its so specific, point to where it says its themed about ignoring rules. And again, point to me where it says that Awkaned themes should trump Lost themes. Give proof of these magic items from a book. I don't believe you, and I'm not just going to take your word. Good day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T16:40:22-07:00","id":1072242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1072229#post1072229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If its so specific, point to where it says its themed about ignoring rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gave a fairly broad short list earlier on, but\u2026<br /> <br /> If &quot;Awakened magic that directly influences the world starts with a Practice that makes things do what they might normally do, then opens up the ability to more fully control a subject, then gets into granting a subject properties it doesn't normally have, then lets you convert a subject into something else entirely, and finally allows you to create or destroy a target phenomenon wholesale in defiance of conservation&quot;<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> &quot;Four out of the ten Arcana grant Attainments at Adeptitude that can be summarized as 'spend a point of Mana to ignore this effect'&quot;<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> &quot;Archmastery is typically sought in the interest of overriding a rule that Mastery of at least one Arcanum and Adeptitude in several more cannot accomplish&quot;<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> &quot;The Phenomenal World is presided over by reality-tyrants that don't want anyone but their chosen elect to Ascend&quot;<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> &quot;Our souls are expert escape artists; it's why we Awaken&quot;<br /> <br /> \u2026don't all point to a pretty clear thematic note of Mage that summarizes to &quot;pursuit of mystical power as pursuit of freedom and the terrible things that exist before, during, and after that process,&quot; then sure, we have nothing more to say to each other on this topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And again, point to me where it says that Awkaned themes should trump Lost themes. </div> </div> </div>You are literally the only one who has been contending that &quot;Masters of the Fate Arcanum can Make an Iris between the Hedge and the material world&quot; is a case of Lost's themes being trumped at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Give proof of these magic items from a book. </div> </div> </div>They're travel tokens from pages 96 and 97 of Equinox Road.<br /> <br /> Your turn: Give proof from a book that the Gentry are actually forbidden from forming a gate out of the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T17:25:34-07:00","id":1072258,"title":"","content":"Can't we just say mages powerful enough can screw with the Hedge if they want to, in the sense that nothing stops them rules-wise, but the narrative consequences make wise (and Wise) mages think twice before they do?<br /> <br /> It doesn't seem too different from mages Shielding vampires from sunlight. Sure, you can do it... but would you really want to, considering all the attention and complications that'll break out once word gets on the streets?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T20:51:41-07:00","id":1072346,"title":"","content":"Assuming it isn't changing in 2e, the only stipulation when it came to leaving the Hedge was that you <i>had</i> to leave through a Hedge Gate. It didn't forbid people from <i>creating</i> Hedge Gates as far as I recall, so leaving by a self created Hedge Gate is still abiding by all of the Hedges rules isn't it? Also, has it even been specified that that rule is even still active?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T23:12:17-07:00","id":1072373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1071975#post1071975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ah, but the problem is that Mage themes shouldn't ignore the themes of Changeling either. Why should Mage's themes ignore Changeling's? Or should Awakened magic be able to ignore rules more than a Demon's?<br /> <br /> As I said before, in 1e, no one could open a gateway out of the Hedge. Not changelings, not the Gentry, not the goblins. In 1e was described as a massive Contract (or other form of pledge magic) with the Hedge itself. And there's lines in 2e that suggest that this is still true. &quot;The Lost can enter the Hedge through any door in the human world. They must leave through established entrances and exits, though.&quot; And we have: &quot;There aren\u2019t a lot of hard rules in the Hedge. But these few things are always true: \u2022 It\u2019s always easy to get lost in the Hedge.&quot; And that rule applies to Gentry, Huntsmen, goblin, changeling, mortal and others alike.<br /> <br /> A mage could, in theory, open a gate, but they'd have to beat a Clash of Wills against the god-level being who's established that Contract in the Hedge, and good luck with that. We have precident for this kind of thing as well (re: altering angels). Now, that might have changed in 2e, and its very possible it has. But until we see something to that effect, I'm going to go with the hints we've seen in Changeling and Demon (re: Rip the Gates).</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno about all that. The more I've thought about it, the more I think as a GM I'd allow the conjuring but present a REACTION from the Hedge. I mean, the Hedge has rules, but unlike some places its rules can and often are broken. The Hedge deliberately doesn't make them ironclad. There are just consequences. You can step off the path if you want, and the Thorns will prick you. I think the Hedge might be better represented as not denying a powerful Mage the opportunity to enact his rule breaking magic. I think the Hedge will just see that he regrets it. Not sure how that plays out in rules, but that's my thought. <br /> <br /> Also, it occurs to me that the overall affect of conjuring up an Iris might be more dramatic and unexpected. I mean...the Hedge is psychosomatic, right? Its shaped by the emotions, dreams and natures of the things moving through it. The general rule of thumb is that the Hedge gets stranger the deeper in you go, presumably in part because the glamour starts to come more from dreams and inhuman thoughts rather than what might leak in from the mortal world. Both bending the usual way of things to get that exit and flooding a perhaps &quot;flooding&quot; a wilder part of the hedge with glamour leaking in through a gate from the mortal world could very likely cause the land to shift in unexpected ways. Night becomes day, stars move in the heavens, seas crash, forests wilt and die or come to a quaking life, so on. Stranger and horrific species of Hobgoblin may spontaneously come into being. You know...the usual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T05:13:11-07:00","id":1072459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1072242#post1072242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gave a fairly broad short list earlier on, but\u2026<br /> \u2026don't all point to a pretty clear thematic note of Mage that summarizes to &quot;pursuit of mystical power as pursuit of freedom and the terrible things that exist before, during, and after that process,&quot; then sure, we have nothing more to say to each other on this topic.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure, I'll agree to that. The only line that's about actually breaking magical rules refers to Archmastery, and that's blindingly obvious. Any tier 4 game critter (archmaster, totem, methusalha, True Fae, archangels) is going to break rules.<br /> <br /> Your mage is about breaking rules. I disagree that Mage as a whole is about breaking rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are literally the only one who has been contending that &quot;Masters of the Fate Arcanum can Make an Iris between the Hedge and the material world&quot; is a case of Lost's themes being trumped at all. </div> </div> </div> Appeal to popularity is a logical fallacy. And I may be the only one who brought up Lost's themes, but others have brought up Mage's themes as if its an excuse to do whatever they want. You need to look at both sides, not just one, or its nothing more than more than bias.<br /> <br /> Travel tokens are designed to bypass the Hedge entirely. They have literally <i>nothing to do with the Hedge by design</i>. The Hedge is its own realm with its own rules. It is not part of Faerie proper. You can make gateways into and out of Faerie. But this and that are separate matters; you have no support for your Hedge-gate claim.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">My turn? Sure. Lets start with the fact that abilities are additive, not assumed. No where does it say Gentry can open gates from inside the Hedge. No power exists. Prior to Equinox Roads, the True Fae used same stats as changelings, just with a few tweaks with Virtue/Vice and time in reality. Equinox Road establishes these as Actors, and the actual True Fae stay in Faerie proper. However, that is meaningless distinction - the True Fae that might appear in the Hedge are all the actors restricted to the same power sets as Changelings (ER p90, bottom left), even if they are just all actors. Omnipotence Constrained (ER p89) talks about how each manifestation of the Gentry, be it Realm or Actor or prop or whisp, must be limited in its abilities to the chosen form. No form it can take has access to hedge gate construction abilities. It can open a gate from inside Faerie, but then, what fae can't? Getting into the Hedge is easy.<br /> <br /> Books talks about these Actors using Hedge gates as normal, traveling on Trods to get there. It talks about the inability of Exiles to enter into Faerie again - if they could just open a gate anywhere, this wouldn't be an issue. The Fae traveling through trods to get to reality is established as a major major dangers of the Hedge. If they could open gates, this would not be an issue. The &quot;Journey to Arcadia&quot; section of ER starting on page 96 all includes hedge travel, save travel tokens, and those are from Ironside to Faerie and back, no Hedge.<br /> <br /> Lets talk about how, in exchange for their power, the Gentry are absolutely bound by the laws of the fae (ER p84). This includes the laws of the Hedge, of which we know that &quot;you must exit through a proper gate&quot; is one of them; it may be established in the Mage section, but its also been established through others as well, so we know its there. They are literally unable to disobey the laws without destroying parts of themselves (names or titles). </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-03-2017, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T05:17:17-07:00","id":1072462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1072346#post1072346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming it isn't changing in 2e, the only stipulation when it came to leaving the Hedge was that you <i>had</i> to leave through a Hedge Gate. It didn't forbid people from <i>creating</i> Hedge Gates as far as I recall, so leaving by a self created Hedge Gate is still abiding by all of the Hedges rules isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div> If that was true, then Rip the Gates and Awakened magic would work. Its forbidden the creation of gates or teleportation out of the hedge. At least from hedgeside. Getting into the hedge by creation of a new gate or teleportation is allowed all the time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T07:01:58-07:00","id":1072507,"title":"","content":"To <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a> and everyone else still on this line of discussions: just what part of Changeling's themes break when a non-changeling gets a not-so-available way to get in and out of the Hedge with relative ease? No sarcasm attempted, just honest curiosity here.<br /> <br /> Is it about the breaking of laws that all fairy creatures are supposed to abide? But isn't that the exact reason for bringing in non-fairy crreatures to the equation? For clever ways to bypass the laws without breaking it, just as tricksters often do?<br /> <br /> Is it about the Hedge's purpose inflicting and reminding of pain? But if someone needs something from the Hedge, wouldn't they delve deep into it enough to hurt themselves anyway?<br /> <br /> <br /> And I just came back from reading the text on Rip the Gates and its sidebar. It says about the God-Machine being more limited in such otherworldly places, and I think that's the main reason why this Exploit fails in the Hedge. It's the lack of the Machine's influence, not the influence of the Hedge, that prohibits forming a gate within the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T10:05:55-07:00","id":1072593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1072462#post1072462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If that was true, then Rip the Gates and Awakened magic would work. Its forbidden the creation of gates or teleportation out of the hedge. At least from hedgeside. Getting into the hedge by creation of a new gate or teleportation is allowed all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it is impossible for magic to take you out of the Hedge without following proper procedure. You can't use Space to create a portal out or Death/Spirit to leave via Twilight. It says you can only leave via a &quot;proper Gateway&quot;, which is described as:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> a doorway, mirror or other aperture made available to access the Hedge through Glamour </div> </div> </div>Which is something Mages, at least in 2e, are capable of creating. They can make a proper Hedge Gate, satisfying the Hedges requirements, since they'd be leaving through a &quot;proper Gateway&quot;. And I'm fairly sure there is absolutely no rule stating that mages can't create Hedge Gates, so everything plays out fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 04-03-2017, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T13:52:44-07:00","id":1072689,"title":"","content":"What happens when mages and fae come into conflict isn't so much Wyrd forcing people into line with a story, as it is the fact that there's this whole world of people and things who rely on intricate bargains and who get really cross when you disrupt that balance. And the most powerful ones don't have any ethical problem replacing your son with a thing that has to sew on its button-eyes every morning but thinks they're just glasses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 04-03-2017, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T11:21:47-07:00","id":1077087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1067106-mages-in-the-hedge?p=1072689#post1072689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when mages and fae come into conflict isn't so much Wyrd forcing people into line with a story, as it is the fact that there's this whole world of people and things who rely on intricate bargains and who get really cross when you disrupt that balance. And the most powerful ones don't have any ethical problem replacing your son with a thing that has to sew on its button-eyes every morning but thinks they're just glasses.</div> </div> </div> </div> Chilling. This is why Mages usually don't mess with the Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}